<concept id="t00104">
	<title>Power sunshade</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>panorama sunroof
					<indexterm>power sunshade</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00543">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00544">
								<image href="images/N_SP3i26_B04_026_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e00545">
								<image href="images/N_SP3i26_B04_027_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Use the power sunshade to block direct sunlight coming through the sunroof glass.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>Push the sunroof switch backward to the first position. The power sunshade slides open.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Push the sunroof switch forward to the first position. The power sunshade closes. The glass closes first if the sunroof is already open.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>To stop the power sunshade at any point, push the sunroof switch in any direction.</p>
		<note type="note">
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>Do not pull or push the power sunshade by hand, as this may damage the power sunshade or cause it to malfunction.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Wrinkles that form on the shade are normal for the material used.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
	</conbody>
